  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The figure shows a circuit having eight resistances of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></math> each, labelled <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math>, and two ideal batteries with voltages <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&epsilon;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&epsilon;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0002_d14e8bf180ca.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 220px;\" /></p><p>Which of the following statement(s) is(are) correct?</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of current flowing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of current flowing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of current flowing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnitude of current flowing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.",
      "is_correct": true
    }
